/-! # Factory glue for the Eighth source (gident2)

The short block of gforest's `eighthSrcVecW` (a triality image, `twTriVec`) has all values
multiples of `256`.  It is given here as packed literal lists of the values divided by `256`
(8-bit fields): pair terms (`eighthPS`), octad blocks (`eighthOctS`) and the odd terms column by
column (`eighthCS0` to `eighthCS23`, checked at width `32`).  The vector `eighthSrcVecS w` (scale
`1 / 32`, tensor columns of width `w`) represents family representative `7` for `w ≥ 31`
(`eighthSrcS_rep`): its short block agrees with the one of `eighthSrcVecW 32`, whose real short
block is the one of `eighthSrcVecW w`, and `IdentVec.real_scale` moves the factor `256` into the
scale.  The numeric tensor bound and the integer matrix glue complete the factory interface. -/

